Privacy Policy for Table to Markdown
Effective Date: 18.03.2026
Last Updated: 18.03.2026

This Privacy Policy explains how Krokit Club ("we", "us", or "our") collects, uses, and protects information when you use the Table to Markdown Google Workspace Add-on (the "Add-on").

By installing or using the Add-on, you agree to this Privacy Policy.

1. Overview

Table to Markdown is designed to convert table data from Google Sheets into Markdown format for productivity and documentation purposes.

We are committed to limiting data access to only what is necessary for the Add-on to function.

2. Information We Access

To provide its functionality, the Add-on may access the following information:

Google Sheets table data that you choose to process with the Add-on;

basic technical information necessary for the Add-on to run within Google Workspace;

limited usage-related information, such as error logs or diagnostic data, if needed to maintain or improve functionality.

The Add-on does not access your data unless it is required to perform the requested conversion.

3. How We Use Information

We use accessed information only for the following purposes:

to read selected table content from Google Sheets;

to generate Markdown output requested by the user;

to maintain, secure, and improve the Add-on;

to detect, prevent, or address technical issues.

We do not use your Google Sheets data for advertising purposes.

4. Data Storage and Retention

The Add-on is intended to process data only as needed to provide the requested conversion.

We do not claim ownership of your spreadsheet data.

We do not sell, rent, or trade your data.

If any technical logs or temporary processing records are created for security, debugging, or service reliability purposes, they are limited to what is reasonably necessary and retained only for as long as needed for those purposes.

5. Data Sharing

We do not sell or share your Google Sheets content with third parties except in the following limited circumstances:

when required by law, regulation, legal process, or governmental request;

when necessary to protect our rights, security, or operations;

when necessary to prevent fraud, abuse, or technical misuse.

6. Third-Party Services

The Add-on operates within Google Workspace and may rely on Google infrastructure and services.

Your use of Google services is subject to Google’s own terms and privacy practices. We are not responsible for Google’s independent handling of data.

7. Data Security

We take reasonable administrative, technical, and organizational measures to protect information processed through the Add-on.

However, no method of electronic transmission or storage is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.

8. User Control

You control whether to install, use, or uninstall the Add-on.

You may stop using the Add-on at any time by uninstalling it from your Google Workspace environment.

Because your spreadsheet content remains under your control within Google services, you remain responsible for the data you choose to process with the Add-on.

9. Children’s Privacy

The Add-on is not directed to children, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children through the Add-on.

10. Changes to This Privacy Policy

We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we do, we will revise the "Last Updated" date above.

Your continued use of the Add-on after any update means you accept the revised Privacy Policy.

